 \section{Discussion and Limitations}
-The central design hypothesis is that typed dependency evidence can constrain
-multi-knob recommendations while an LLM may help combine unfamiliar telemetry
-and explain the result. The planned matched ablation is necessary to determine
-whether the LLM adds recommendation quality beyond rules, BO, RL, or graph
-lookup; explanation fluency alone is not evidence of optimization value.
+\label{sec:discussion}
+The central idea remains the separation of structured evidence, proposals, and enforcement. The current artifact demonstrates a dry-run decision contract and auditable baseline and per-process intervention measurements, not end-to-end kernel optimization. It lacks a deployed bundle actuator, traffic isolation, measured graph induction, a verified trained checkpoint, and controlled end-to-end comparative results. Prompting a model to obey graph edges does not enforce those edges; independent validation is required. The current runtime enforces only its explicit example constraints.
 
-The dependency graph records observed associations, not causal couplings.
-Retrieved evidence may be stale, uncertainty may be miscalibrated under drift,
-and staging can expose canary traffic before rollback. Accordingly, the safety
-runtime is defense in depth rather than a correctness proof. Generality is also
-unestablished until held-out workload-family experiments are completed from
-traceable hardware logs. Production deployments, hard-real-time systems, and
-cross-kernel portability remain future work.
+The available telemetry prototype contains scheduler and block-I/O demonstration proxies, including timestamp-derived buckets; those are not end-to-end request latencies. They must not calibrate an empirical SLO claim. Actual workload drivers must record completion, failure and deadline data. The new local benchmarks do so for their narrow tasks but do not substitute for web serving, TPC-C, Kafka/Spark, GPU inference or audio pipelines.
+
+The rank gate's assumptions can fail under drift, selective labeling, or a score model updated using calibration data. A canary can suffer harm before detection, and rollback cannot undo every side effect. No no-worse-than-default, catastrophic-regression prevention, Pareto superiority or universal safety claim follows from the prototype. These limitations define concrete measurements and engineering prerequisites for the next evaluation.
